# Mens Culture — project context

Simple **one-page** marketing site for a men's hairdresser: who they are, what they do, and a link to book on a **third-party platform** (not built on this site). A password-protected `/admin` area lets the owner manage a single promo banner shown under the sticky header.

## In the repo today

| Layer | Choice |
|---|---|
| Framework | Next.js 16 (App Router) |
| UI | React 19, Tailwind CSS v4 |
| Data | Neon Postgres, Drizzle ORM (`neon-http`), Zod (see **`database`**) |
| Tooling | Biome, ESLint (`eslint-config-next`), Husky, commitlint, lint-staged |
| Package manager | pnpm |

## Layout

- **Path aliases** in [`tsconfig.json`](../../tsconfig.json): `@components` → `app/_components/index.ts`, `@utils` → `app/_utils/index.ts`; `@/*` for other roots.
- App routes live under [`app/`](../../app/) (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `globals.css`). Non-route folders under `app/` use a **`_` prefix** (see **`code-hygiene`**).
- Import shared UI/helpers as `from "@components"` / `from "@utils"`. Server Actions → `app/_actions/`.
- Server-only code lives at the repo root: `db/` (Drizzle client, schema, `queries/`) and `lib/` (`env.ts`, `session.ts`, `rateLimit.ts`, `validations/`). Import via `@/db/...` and `@/lib/...`.

## Product guardrails (when building features)

- Primary **Book** action goes to the external booking URL — stay consistent (same tab vs new tab).
- Keep the page **fast, accessible, and mobile-first**. Meet **WCAG 2.2 Level AA** (see **`accessibility`**).
- **Website copy** (headings, body text, buttons, `metadata`, image `alt` text, and strings in `app/_constants/` meant for the public site): do **not** use the em dash (—). Prefer a full stop, comma, colon, or parentheses (e.g. rewrite two clauses as separate sentences or use “:” before a list).
